  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "If a worker receives a \\(20\\) percent cut in wages, he may regain his original pay exactly by obtaining a raise of:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(20\\) percent",
    "B": "\\(25\\) percent",
    "C": "\\(22\\dfrac12\\) percent",
    "D": "\\(\\$20\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$25\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Let the original wage be \\(w>0\\). After the \\(20\\%\\) cut, the wage is \\(0.8w\\), so restoring the original pay requires an increase of \\(0.2w\\).\n\nThe raise percentage is measured against the current wage, which is \\(0.8w\\). Therefore the required rate is\n\\[\n\\frac{0.2w}{0.8w}=\\frac14=25\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{25\\%}\\), choice B.",
